.TH HASHCAT 1 "" "hashcat" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hashcat \- advanced password recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashcat
[options]... hash|hashfile|hccapxfile [dictionary|mask|directory]...
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-hash\-type " Num"
Hash\-type, references below (otherwise autodetect)
.br
Example: \-m 1000
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-recipe " Str"
Hash recipe for hash\-mode 4000
.br
Example: \-\-hash\-recipe 'md5(md5(salt) . pass)'
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-attack\-mode " Num"
Attack\-mode, see references below
.br
Example: \-a 3
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help. Use \-hh to show all supported hash\-modes
.br
Example: \-h or \-hh
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress output
.TP
.B \-\-hex\-charset
Assume charset is given in hex
.TP
.B \-\-hex\-salt
Assume salt is given in hex
.TP
.B \-\-hex\-wordlist
Assume words in wordlist are given in hex
.TP
.B \-\-force
Ignore warnings
.TP
.B \-\-deprecated\-check\-disable
Enable deprecated plugins
.TP
.B \-\-pipeline\-stats
Show where each launch's time goes, per device
.TP
.B \-\-task\-time\-breakdown
Show where the run's wall clock went, by stage
.TP
.B \-\-status
Enable automatic update of the status screen
.TP
.B \-\-status\-json
Enable JSON format for status output
.TP
.B \-\-json
Enable JSON format for all output
.TP
.B \-\-status\-timer " Num"
Sets seconds between status screen updates to X
.br
Example: \-\-status\-timer=1
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-count " Num"
Expected number of lines on stdin, for the ETA
.br
Example: \-\-stdin\-count=1000000
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-timeout\-abort " Num"
Abort if there is no input from stdin for X seconds
.br
Example: \-\-stdin\-timeout\-abort=300
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-timeout\-flush " Num"
Crack a partial batch after X idle seconds on stdin
.br
Example: \-\-stdin\-timeout\-flush=5
.TP
.B \-\-machine\-readable
Display the status view in a machine\-readable format
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-guessing
Keep guessing the hash after it has been cracked
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test\-disable
Disable self\-test functionality on startup
.TP
.B \-\-loopback
Add new plains to induct directory
.TP
.B \-\-markov\-hcstat2 " File"
Specify hcstat2 file to use
.br
Example: \-\-markov\-hcstat2=my.hcstat2
.TP
.B \-\-markov\-disable
Disables markov\-chains, emulates classic brute\-force
.TP
.B \-\-markov\-classic
Enables classic markov\-chains, no per\-position
.TP
.B \-\-markov\-inverse
Enables inverse markov\-chains, no per\-position
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-markov\-threshold " Num"
Threshold X when to stop accepting new markov\-chains
.br
Example: \-t 50
.TP
.B \-\-metal\-compiler\-runtime " Num"
Abort Metal kernel build after X seconds of runtime
.br
Example: \-\-metal\-compiler\-runtime=180
.TP
.B \-\-runtime " Num"
Abort session after X seconds of runtime
.br
Example: \-\-runtime=10
.TP
.B \-\-session " Str"
Define specific session name
.br
Example: \-\-session=mysession
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Show the command line to resume \-\-session, then stop
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-disable
Do not write restore file
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-file\-path " File"
Specific path to restore file
.br
Example: \-\-restore\-file\-path=x.restore
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-position
Take only the position from the restore file
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-outfile " File"
Define outfile for recovered hash
.br
Example: \-o outfile.txt
.TP
.B \-\-outfile\-format " Str"
Outfile format to use, separated with commas
.br
Example: \-\-outfile\-format=1,3
.TP
.B \-\-outfile\-json
Force JSON format in outfile format
.TP
.B \-\-outfile\-autohex\-disable
Disable the use of $HEX[] in output plains
.TP
.B \-\-outfile\-check\-timer " Num"
Sets seconds between outfile checks to X
.br
Example: \-\-outfile\-check\-timer=30
.TP
.B \-\-wordlist\-autohex\-disable
Disable the conversion of $HEX[] from the wordlist
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-separator " Char"
Separator char for hashlists and outfile
.br
Example: \-p :
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Do not crack a hash, instead print candidates only
.TP
.B \-\-show
Compare hashlist with potfile; show cracked hashes
.TP
.B \-\-left
Compare hashlist with potfile; show uncracked hashes
.TP
.B \-\-username
Enable ignoring of usernames in hashfile
.TP
.B \-\-dynamic\-x
Load hashes written in John's $dynamic_X$ format
.TP
.B \-\-remove
Enable removal of hashes once they are cracked
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-timer " Num"
Update input hash file each X seconds
.br
Example: \-\-remove\-timer=30
.TP
.B \-\-potfile\-disable
Do not write potfile
.TP
.B \-\-potfile\-path " File"
Specific path to potfile
